  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "NORM.DIST and NORMDIST densities store x87 z, divide EXP(-z^2/2) by stdev before 1/sqrt(2*pi), and flush subnormals",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, NORM.DIST(x, mean, stdev, cumulative) and NORMDIST evaluate cumulative = TRUE as NORM.S.DIST((x - mean) / stdev, TRUE) in binary64, whereas for cumulative = FALSE they compute z = RN53(RN64(RN53(RN64(x - mean)) / stdev)), square z in x87 (returning #NUM! on overflow), compute EXP(-sq / 2), divide by stdev BEFORE multiplying by RN(1/sqrt(2*pi)) = 0x3fd9884533d43651, and flush subnormal outputs to +0. Under compat-1, @NORM.DIST returns #NAME? while NORMDIST remains available.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20430 (24,246/24,246 NORM.DIST and 4,510/4,510 NORMDIST full-bank rows; 120/120 pinned each) and 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (rows 161, 165) and jnt_w111_text_dates.",
